sociation":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Terms and Conditions\n\n- [x] I agree to the [Grant Agreement](https://9ba4718c-5c73-47c3-a024-4fc4e5278803.usrfiles.com/ugd/9ba471_f81ef4e4b5f040038350270590eb2e42.pdf) terms if funded\n- [x] I agree to [Provide KYC information](https://9ba4718c-5c73-47c3-a024-4fc4e5278803.usrfiles.com/ugd/9ba471_7d9e73d16b584a61bae92282b208efc4.pdf) if funded above $50,000 USD\n- [x] I agree to disclose conflicts of interest\n- [x] I agree to adhere to the [Code of Conduct](https://forum.zcashcommunity.com/t/zcg-code-of-conduct/41787) and [Communication Guidelines](https://forum.zcashcommunity.com/t/zcg-communication-guidelines/44284)\n- [x] I understand all milestone deliverables will be validated and accepted by their intended users or their representatives, who will confirm that the deliverables meet the required quality, functionality, and usability for each user story.\n- [x] I agree that for any new open-source software, I will create a `CONTRIBUTING.md` file that reflects the high standards of Zcash development, using the [`librustzcash` style guides](https://github.com/zcash/librustzcash/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#styleguides) as a primary reference.\n- [x] I understand when contributing to existing Zcash code, I am required to adhere to the project specific contribution guidelines, paying close attention to any [merge](https://github.com/zcash/librustzcash/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#merge-workflow), [branch](https://github.com/zcash/librustzcash/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#branch-history), [pull request](https://github.com/zcash/librustzcash/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#pull-request-review), and [commit](https://github.com/zcash/librustzcash/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#commit-messages) guidelines as exemplified in the `librustzcash` repository.\n- [x] I agree to post request details on the [Community Forum](https://forum.zcashcommunity.com/c/grants/33)\n- [x] I understand it is my responsibility to post a link to this issue on the [Zcash Community Forums](https://forum.zcashcommunity.com/c/grants/33) after this application has been submitted so the community can give input. I understand this is required in order for ZCG to discuss and vote on this grant application.\n\n### Application Owners (@Octocat, @Octocat1)\n\n@dismad @zksquirrel @vitozkp @onajifortune @theKroy\n\n### Organization Name\n\nZecHub\n\n### How did you learn about Zcash Community Grants\n\nBeing Active Zcash Community Members\n\n### Requested Grant Amount (USD)\n\n419361.00\n\n### Category\n\nEducation\n\n### Project Lead\n\n```project-lead.yaml\nName: zksquirrel\nRole: Core Contributor\nBackground: Zcash Arborist Community Notetaker,and ZKAV Club Team Member\nResponsibilities: Operations, Comms, Education\n```\n\n### Additional Team Members\n\n```team-members.yaml\n- Name: dismad\n   Role: Core Contributor\n   Background: Mathematics, Computer Science, and Education. Cypherpunkzero holder, Discord Moderator, experience in the Automotive Industry for 15+ years\n   Responsibilities: Technical, Governance, Education\n- Name: vitozkp\n   Role: Core Contributor\n   Background: Zcash Discord Administrator. Previous reviews, sponsored articles, opinions, and much more about the digital world. Digital Editor.\n   Responsibilities: Media Editor, Community, Social media\n- Name: onajifortune\n   Role: Core Contributor\n   Background: Software Developer and active open-source contributor with a strong focus on problem-solving, rapid prototyping, and practical implementation. I am also a Graduate Electronic and Electrical Engineer.\n   Responsibilities: Developer\n- Name: theKroy\n   Role: Core Contributor\n   Background:  Multidisciplinary Graphic Designer with 7+ years of experience and proficiency with Adobe CC programs; Photoshop, Illustrator, and InDesign. Specialty in Visual Brand Identity and Layout Design. Designer of Zkool's offical logo.\n   Responsibilities: Designer\n```\n\n### Project Summary\n\nThis proposal seeks to grow Zcash’s open-source education hub and\nonboard more contributors to Zcash.\n\n### Project Description\n\n## Previous Achievements\n\n* Over the past 3 years we have onboarded 232 new Zcash contributors and have grown a lively community on Twitter, Discord, and Matrix. \n* We have formed parnerships with several other privacy projects including Nym, Namada, Penumbra, Pirate Chain, Decred, and Dash.\n* We hosted numerious events including: 2x Zcash Birthdays, Community/Governance Calls, and restreaming live events.\n* Have grown the ZecHub DAO to 26 members whom govern the projects direction\n* Hit over 1000 subscribers on our YouTube channel providing tutorials, podcasts, shorts, and collaborative content\n* Weekly digest readers has grown to 451 subscribers ( over 71,000 views since we started! )\n* We have help fund 6 successfull Ambassador projects across the globe in 2025\n* Over 4k Discord users\n* Over the year on Twitter, we have achieved 1.3 million impressions and 65.3k engagements with our posts\n* On DAODAO we executed 123 proposals since we started\n* We processed 316 shielded payments to contributors in 2025 via FPF\n\n\n\n## Areas of Focus for 2026\n\n* Ecosystem communication\n* Developer discovery\n* Governance exploration\n* Education expansion\n\n\nHere are some more details on areas we plan to focus on:\n\n### ZecHub Visual Brand Identity\n\nWe plan to create a ZecHub Visual brand identity that will contain ZecHub branded assets and help achieve clear recognition and a more professional outlook on all platforms.\n\n### New Zec Bounties Platform\n\nWe plan to fully develop the ZEC Bounty platform and move away from Dework in 2026. This will allow us shielded ZEC directly with our bounties and streamline our processes. We will also create the platform such that other projects like Namada or Penumbra could fork and use it as well.\n\n\n### Zcash Ecosystem Digest & Newsletter\n\nOur newsletter helps keep the community up-to-date on everything going on. Zcash is MUCH bigger now with many diverse and independent teams working across the globe. We offer our newsletter shielded, and also in more traditional venues like substack.\n\n### ZecHub DAO\n\nWe intend to be the first public Zcash DAO to openly use FROST for our wallet operations. We will also experiment with new governance technologies that help us find consensus. We encourage anyone in the community to get involved, learning happens best with engagement. The DAO will manage community proposals that are submitted. The ZecHub DAO is a great way for new developers and/or educators to get involved from the ground level.\n\n### ZecHub Podcast\n\nThroughout the year we intend to continue bringing on knowledgeable guests from Privacy Projects. Educating on new platforms, building context and understanding around technologies complementary to Zcash. \n\n### ZecHub Tutorials\n\nWe will continue to produce timely educational tutorials for the community. \n\nWe will be using Premiere Pro and other software to improve the quality of the editing, including audio and animations\n\nReach out for ideas if content you want is not available.\n\n\n\n### ZecHub Collaborations\n\nWe will reach out to existing education platforms like Khan Academy in a effort to disseminate Zcash and privacy related material. We will also continue to build relationships and engage with aligned communities. We will also participate in all ecosystem workshops to spearhead the educational needs of the community.\n\n\n### ZecHub Wiki Delegation\n\nWe intend to hand-off ZecHub wiki operations to DAO members. Every DAO member will be given access to the github in an effort to further decentralize our work. Core contributors will oversee any issues should they arise. \n\n#### ZecHub Dashboard Management\n\nWe will continue to manage the more technical areas of data that is collected. This includes:\n\n1. Run and maintain Zebrad/zcashd nodes\n2. Respond to new data needs from the community \n3. Fix/report bugs \n4. Stay up-to-date with changes with the new Z3 stack\n\n\n\n\n### Arborist Call Recap Management\n\nWe will help manage all aspects of the biweekly Arborist calls. This includes:\n\n1. Notetaking\n2. Short clip creation ( with subtitles)\n3. Social Media threads\n\n\n### ZecHub Voting Authority\n\nWe will commit to running as a Voting Authority for all elections in 2026. This includes:\n\n1.) Run and maintaining a server used to run `zcash-vote-server` and `cometbft` as needed\n2.) Renew and use the `zecvote.zone` domain ( if needed)\n3.) Hold workshops before each election teaching/training those who need assistance with becoming a vote authority. This will aid in creating good up to date documentation that community can use.\n4.) Work with Hahn,ZCG, and the community to report bugs and communicate issues as they arise\n\n\n### ZecHub Hackathons\n\nThis year we propose to host 2 hackathons to maximize our impact in growing Zcash developer excitement. \n\n\n>Onboarding new developers is the biggest opportunity for growth within the Zcash ecosystem.\n\n\nZecHub is uniquely positioned to find and fund smaller devs/projects that may fall between the cracks. We love working from the ground up.\n\n### ZecHub Store Management\n\nWe plan to manage https://zechub.store/ throughout 2026. We proudly accept shielded ZEC. Its important we lead by example when selling our merch! Designs come from community members and all ZEC received is purposed toward Zcash education. We currently use ZGO for shielded payments.\n\n### Namada Validator\n\nWe plan to continue to operate our ZecHub Validator for Namada as a way to bridge our two communities and learn from one another. It will also potentially provide a source of income for the DAO.\n\n### My First Zcash ( MFZ )\n\nWe plan to take over the MFZ project and manage it through to publishing of v2 with engaged contributors and/or DAO members. We have already secured the needed domain names for 2026.\n\n### Other\n\nWe also want to hear from you, the community. What would you like us to focus on moving into 2026? Part of what makes ZecHub work so well is our ground level work that really listens to members in the community.\n\n### Proposed Problem\n\nThe Zcash ecoystem is rapidly growing fullstop. Various aspects of the ecoystem are developing quickly and must be understood by the community in realtime. In addition, the technical nature of Zcash may introduce misunderstandings and through widely available educational resources these can be eliminated. There is also a need for an indepdendent group to test new ecosystem infrastructure as necessary.  Zcash users span the globe and having a single resource where folks can convene and engage in discussion is important. Coordinating and assisting Core orgs and global communities towards community events.\n\nAs Zcash is growing we need to find new developrs, designers, and other contributors bringing in useful skills and talents. It is also neccessary to demonstrate real world usage of shielded ZEC as a means of payment. At present, several privacy aligned projects exists in the ecoystem and a team is needed to perform outreach and engage with and promote the idea that privacy is a fundamental human right.\n\n\n### Proposed Solution\n\nOur role in the ecosystem is to consistently provide interesting educational content through a Weekly Ecosystem Digest, Wallet Demos, Video Explainers, Twitter Posts and Events. ZecHub also serves as a open meeting place for community member planning and discussions.\n\n### Solution Format\n\nThe format of the work will be:\n\nMonthly milestone recaps with KPI's on the Zcash community forum\nEcosytem presence / communication\nDiscord Office hours\nZcash wiki\nWeekly Zcash Ecosystem Digest\nConsistent Zcash education via Social Media channels\nVideo Explainers, Community Events, Podcasts, X Spaces, Zcash Wallet Demos\nWiki Site Documentation\nZcash Network Metrics\nWritten Articles about Zcash\n\n- ZecHub Hackathon(s) 2026\n   - 60% of Bounty fund ( 60 ZEC )\n   - Higher payout to encourage more development work\n   \n- Ambassadors Initiatives\n   - 20% of Bounty fund ( 20 ZEC )\n   - Proposal to DAO required\n   - Monthly recap on Zcash Community Forum required\n\n- ZecHub Community Proposals\n   - 10% of Bounty fund ( 10 ZEC )\n   - DAO votes on every proposal\n\n- Small Bounty Fund\n   - 10% of Bounty fund ( 10 ZEC )\n   - Dev work: 0.12 to 0.5 ZEC\n   - Video content - up to 0.15 ZEC per video and/or audio posted on ZecHub \n   - Newsletter - 0.05 ZEC per edition\n   - ZecHub Wiki - 0.08 ZEC per new page published\nsocials\n   - Dev work: 0.12 to 0.5 ZEC\n\n### Dependencies\n\n>What external entities is your project dependent on? What involvement is required from ZF, ECC, and/or other >external organizations? Who would have to incorporate your work in order for it to be usable?\n\nThe podcast and twitter spaces events are dependent on Zcash community members and other projects being open to attending. ZecHub is dependent on its DAO members and open-source contributors to see the platform thrive.\n\n>Execution risks: What obstacles do you expect? What is most likely to go wrong? Which unknown factors could >jeopardize success? Who would have to incorporate your work in order for it to be usable?\n\nThe biggest execution risk would be misallocation of the Bounty Pool. It is vital that ample time is provided for project planning. Specifically Tasks, Services and Events need to be budgeted for in advance.\n\nAnother education risk is the hub’s dependency on one person for media materials. There should be a strong focus on developing more content creators for the hub.\n\n### Technical Approach\n\n* The ZecHub DAO manages all ZEC bounties, while FPF administers the payments. On a weekly basis tasks relevant to Zcash including documenation research, graphic design, and development are listed on dework ( soon to be ZEC bounties app ) , and paid.\n* Durning the week developments in the Zcash ecosystem are collated and sent out via our social media channels to keep the community up-to-date. A summary of developments is created and published.\n   *  Ecoystem Digest\n   *  Shielded News\n\n### ZecHub Wiki\n\n* ZecHub wiki is an open source repository hosted on the ZecHub github. It includes guides, wallets including their features, privacy tools, research, and links to community projects. Brand logos are also available for community projects.\n\n#### Zechub Dashboard\n\n* ZecHub dashboard is an open source Zash data repository hosted on the zechub-wiki github. Zcash node data is upload either daily or weekly depending on the type. It is sourced from a running zebrad node and available in JSON format.\n\n### ZecHub Store\n\n* We proudly use ZGo to accept shielded `ZEC` payments\n* We accept community designs \n* All `ZEC` recieved is used puprosed for Zcash education\n* Provide store support for the ecosystem as needed\n\n### Outreach\n\nWe will build relationships and engage with aligned communities by joining community calls, events, and creating tutorials. We will also participate in all ecosystem workshops to spearhead the educational needs of the community\n\n\n### Community Infra\n\nWe will commit to running as a Voting Authority for all elections in 2026. This includes:\n\n1.) Run and maintaining a server used to run `zcash-vote-server` and `cometbft` as needed\n2.) Renew and use the `zecvote.zone` domain ( if needed)\n3.) Hold workshops before each election teaching/training those who need assistance with becoming a vote authority. This will aid in creating good up to date documentation that community can use.\n4.) Work with Hahn,ZCG, and the community to report bugs and communicate issues as they arise\n\n\n### Media\n\n* YouTube playlists for tutorials, interviews, podcasts, and events.\n* Twitter tutorials\n* Custom motion graphics\n\n\n\n\n\n### Upstream Merge Opportunities\n\nn/a\n\n### Hardware/Software Costs (USD)\n\n0\n\n### Hardware/Software Justification\n\nn/a\n\n### Service Costs (USD)\n\n0\n\n### Service Costs Justification\n\nn/a\n\n### Compensation Costs (USD)\n\n376320.00\n\n### Compensation Costs Justification\n\n```markdown\n    @squirrel   - $65 * 32 hrs  * 48 weeks = $99,840\n    @dismad     - $65 * 32 hrs  * 48 weeks = $99,840\n    @vito       - $45 * 32 hrs  * 48 weeks = $69,120\n    @tron       - $35 * 32 hrs  * 48 weeks = $53,760\n    @Kroy       - $35 * 32 hrs  * 48 weeks = $53,760\n```\n\n### Total Budget (USD)\n\n419361.00\n\n### Previous Funding\n\nYes\n\n### Previous Funding Details\n\n[ZecHub 2025](https://github.com/ZcashCommunityGrants/zcashcommunitygrants/issues/9)\n\n### Other Funding Sources\n\nNo\n\n### Other Funding Sources Details\n\nn/a\n\n### Implementation Risks\n\nThe biggest execution risk would be misallocation of the Bounty Pool. It is vital that ample time is provided for project planning. Specifically Tasks, Services and Events need to be budgeted for in advance.\n\nAnother education risk is the hub’s dependency on one person for media materials. There should be a strong focus on developing more content creators for the hub.\n\n\n### Potential Side Effects\n\nn/a\n\n### Success Metrics\n\nThe main metrics related to ZecHub’s success are social media metrics (followers, video views, newsletter subscribers, etc) and the number of contributors building ZecHub related items. \n\n### Startup Funding (USD)\n\n43041.00\n\n### Startup Funding Justification\n\n### Start up costs:\n\n```markdown\nAdobe CC $69.99 - month / 12x = $840\nCanva: $8 - month / 12x = $96\nLinktree: $5 - month / 12x = $60\nTwitter premium+: $400 year\nWordpress hosting: $300 year\nDocs Collaboration - $200 year\nBusiness License - $300 year\nTailscale Personal Plus - $60 year\nVPS (3 servers) - $1600 year\nMidjourney $30 - month / 12x = $360\nMisc $500\n\n```\n=> $4716\n\n### ZEC Bounty\n\n```markdown\nAdmin fee: - 5 ZEC\n\nWe will follow the below earmarks:\n\n       \n- ZecHub Hackathon(s) 2026\n   - 50% of Bounty fund ( 50 ZEC )\n   - Higher payout to encourage more development work\n   \n- Ambassadors Initiatives\n   - 20% of Bounty fund ( 20 ZEC )\n   - Proposal to DAO required\n   - Monthly recap on Zcash Community Forum required\n\n- ZecHub Community Proposals\n   - 10% of Bounty fund ( 10 ZEC )\n   - DAO votes on every proposal\n\n- Small Bounty Fund\n   - 20% of Bounty fund ( 20 ZEC )\n   - Dev work: 0.12 to 0.5 ZEC\n   - Video content - up to 0.15 ZEC per video and/or audio posted on ZecHub \n   - Newsletter - 0.05 ZEC per edition\n   - ZecHub Wiki - 0.08 ZEC per new page published\nsocials\n   - Dev work: 0.12 to 0.5 ZEC\n   ```\n=> $38,325\n\n### Milestone Details\n\n```milestones.yaml\nMilestone 1 - estimated completion date: 01/31/2026\n\nMilestone 1 - USD value of payout upon completion of deliverables: $31,360\nDeliverable 1.1: ZecHub team report\nMilestone 2 - estimated completion date: 02/28/2026\n\nMilestone 2 - USD value of payout upon completion of deliverables: $31,360\nDeliverable 2.1: ZecHub team report\nMilestone 3 - estimated completion date: 03/31/2026\n\nMilestone 3 - USD value of payout upon completion of deliverables: $31,360\nDeliverable 3.1: ZecHub team report**\nMilestone 4 - estimated completion date: 04/30/2026\n\nMilestone 4 - USD value of payout upon completion of deliverables: $31,360\nDeliverable 4.1: ZecHub team report\nMilestone 5 - estimated completion date: 05/31/2026\n\nMilestone 5 - USD value of payout upon completion of deliverables: $31,360\nDeliverable 5.1: ZecHub team report\nMilestone 6 - estimated completion date: 06/30/2026\n\nMilestone 6 - USD value of payout upon completion of deliverables: $31,360\nDeliverable 6.1: ZecHub team report\nMilestone 7 - estimated completion date: 07/31/2026\n\nMilestone 7 - USD value of payout upon completion of deliverables: $31,360\nDeliverable 7.1: ZecHub team report\nMilestone 8 - estimated completion date: 08/31/2026\n\nMilestone 8 - USD value of payout upon completion of deliverables: $31,360\nDeliverable 8.1: ZecHub team report\nMilestone 9 - estimated completion date: 09/30/2026\n\nMilestone 9 - USD value of payout upon completion of deliverables: $31,360\nDeliverable 9.1: ZecHub team report\nMilestone 10 - estimated completion date: 10/31/2026\n\nMilestone 10 - USD value of payout upon completion of deliverables: $31,360\nDeliverable 10.1: ZecHub team report\nMilestone 11 - estimated completion date: 11/30/2026\n\nMilestone 11 - USD value of payout upon completion of deliverables: $31,360\nDeliverable 11.1: ZecHub team report\nMilestone 12 - estimated completion date: 12/31/2026\n\nMilestone 12 - USD value of payout upon completion of deliverables: $31,360\nDeliverable 12.1: ZecHub team report\n```\n\n### Supporting Documents\n\n```files.yaml\n\n```","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ZcashCommunityGrants/zcashcommunitygrants/issues/153/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ZcashCommunityGrants/zcashcommunitygrants/issues/153/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/muhammadkhawar400-alt/cyber-security-registration/issues/1","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/muhammadkhawar400-alt/cyber-security-registration","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/muhammadkhawar400-alt/cyber-security-registration/issues/1/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/muhammadkhawar400-alt/cyber-security-registration/issues/1/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/muhammadkhawar400-alt/cyber-security-registration/issues/1/events","html_url":"https://github.com/muhammadkhawar400-alt/cyber-security-registration/issues/1","id":4795147856,"node_id":"I_kwDOTLldq88AAAABHdAmUA","number":1,"title":"index.html","user":{"login":"muhammadkhawar400-alt","id":229614460,"node_id":"U_kgDODa-jfA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229614460?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadkhawar400-alt","html_url":"https://github.com/muhammadkhawar400-alt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadkhawar400-alt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadkhawar400-alt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadkhawar400-alt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadkhawar400-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadkhawar400-alt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadkhawar400-alt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadkhawar400-alt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadkhawar400-alt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadkhawar400-alt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-02T14:01:49Z","updated_at":"2026-07-02T14:01:49Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Cyber Skills with Muhammad Khawar</title>\n\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n\n<link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Poppins:wght@300;400;600;700&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\"\nhref=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.2/css/all.min.css\">\n\n</head>\n\n<body>\n\n<header>\n\n<div class=\"logo\">\n\n<h2>🛡 Cyber Skills</h2>\n\n<p>with Muhammad Khawar</p>\n\n</div>\n\n</header>\n\n<section class=\"hero\">\n\n<div class=\"left\">\n\n<h1>Become a Professional Cyber Security Expert</h1>\n\n<p>\n\nLearn Ethical Hacking, Networking, Linux, Web Security,\n\nBug Bounty and Practical Labs.\n\n</p>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"right\">\n\n<form id=\"registrationForm\">\n\n<h2>Student Registration</h2>\n\n<input type=\"text\" placeholder=\"Full Name\" id=\"name\" required>\n\n<input type=\"text\" placeholder=\"City\" id=\"city\" required>\n\n<input type=\"tel\" placeholder=\"WhatsApp Number\" id=\"phone\" required>\n\n<input type=\"email\" placeholder=\"Gmail Address\" id=\"email\" required>\n\n<input type=\"text\" placeholder=\"Education\" id=\"education\" required>\n\n<textarea\nid=\"course\"\nrows=\"5\"\nplaceholder=\"What do you want to learn?\"\nrequired></textarea>\n\n<button type=\"submit\">\n\nRegister Now\n\n</button>\n\n</form>\n\n</div>\n\n</section>\n\n<script src=\"script.js\"></script>\n\n</body>\n\n</html>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/muhammadkhawar400-alt/cyber-security-registration/issues/1/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/muhammadkhawar400-alt/cyber-security-registration/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maciej-or/hikvision_next/issues/246","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maciej-or/hikvision_next","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maciej-or/hikvision_next/issues/246/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maciej-or/hikvision_next/issues/246/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maciej-or/hikvision_next/issues/246/events","html_url":"https://github.com/maciej-or/hikvision_next/issues/246","id":2654844570,"node_id":"I_kwDOI50q1M6ePbaa","number":246,"title":"Video stream not working with HWN-2408MH-8P NVR","user":{"login":"Alfystar","id":32840211,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODQwMjEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32840211?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alfystar","html_url":"https://github.com/Alfystar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alfystar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alfystar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alfystar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alfystar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alfystar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alfystar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alfystar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alfystar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alfystar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":5116522111,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI50q1M8AAAABMPfufw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maciej-or/hikvision_next/labels/help","name":"help","color":"008672","default":false,"description":"Troubleshooting"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":19,"created_at":"2024-11-13T09:35:20Z","updated_at":"2026-07-02T10:54:55Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I have an NVR surveillance system with the model HWN-2408MH-8P. I managed to find the ISAPI access option from the configuration page, but I haven't found a way to access user permissions and haven't yet worked on events.\r\n\r\nWhen integrating the plugin, it immediately identified my 5 cameras by entering the username, password, and URL, showing their names and some status. However, the video stream is \"dead.\" When I try to start it, the screen is gray, and the following error appears in the system log:\r\n\r\n```\r\nLogger: root\r\nSource: components/stream/worker.py:271\r\nFirst occurred: 10:21:02 (2 occurrences)\r\nLast logged: 10:21:18\r\n\r\nUncaught thread exception\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/threading.py\", line 1073, in _bootstrap_inner\r\n    self.run()\r\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/threading.py\", line 1010, in run\r\n    self._target(*self._args, **self._kwargs)\r\n  File \"/usr/src/homeassistant/homeassistant/components/stream/__init__.py\", line 438, in _run_worker\r\n    stream_worker(\r\n  File \"/usr/src/homeassistant/homeassistant/components/stream/worker.py\", line 618, in stream_worker\r\n    muxer.mux_packet(first_keyframe)\r\n  File \"/usr/src/homeassistant/homeassistant/components/stream/worker.py\", line 271, in mux_packet\r\n    self._av_output.mux(packet)\r\n  File \"av/container/output.pyx\", line 218, in av.container.output.OutputContainer.mux\r\n  File \"av/container/output.pyx\", line 224, in av.container.output.OutputContainer.mux_one\r\n  File \"av/container/output.pyx\", line 190, in av.container.output.OutputContainer.start_encoding\r\n  File \"av/container/core.pyx\", line 290, in av.container.core.Container.err_check\r\n  File \"av/error.pyx\", line 336, in av.error.err_check\r\nav.error.ValueError: [Errno 22] Invalid argument: '<none>'; last error log: [mp4] dimensions not set\r\n```\r\n\r\nI couldn't find any similar errors among the issues, but if I missed something, I apologize. I would love to integrate this fantastic plugin into my setup.\r\n\r\n**System Information:**\r\n- Home Assistant Core: 2024.10.4 (Docker installation)\r\n- Frontend: 20241002.4\r\n- hickvision_next: 1.0.19\r\n\r\nI am available for any help and testing. Thanks in advance!","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maciej-or/hikvision_next/issues/246/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maciej-or/hikvision_next/issues/246/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eclipse-rcptt/org.eclipse.rcptt/issues/176","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eclipse-rcptt/org.eclipse.rcptt","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eclipse-rcptt/org.eclipse.rcptt/issues/176/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eclipse-rcptt/org.eclipse.rcptt/issues/176/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eclipse-rcptt/org.eclipse.rcptt/issues/176/events","html_url":"https://github.com/eclipse-rcptt/org.eclipse.rcptt/issues/176","id":3075057547,"node_id":"I_kwDOHRQ7q863SaeL","number":176,"title":"RCPTT model layer is not thread-safe: concurrent access causes spurious exceptions and deadlocks","user":{"login":"basilevs","id":650857,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDg1Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/650857?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilevs","html_url":"https://github.com/basilevs","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilevs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilevs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilevs/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilevs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilevs/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilevs/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilevs/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilevs/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilevs/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":24,"created_at":"2025-05-19T21:27:22Z","updated_at":"2026-07-02T07:09:07Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":{"id":24134727,"node_id":"IT_kwDOCyR8hc4BcERH","name":"Bug","description":"An unexpected problem or behavior","color":"red","created_at":"2024-10-31T14:28:13Z","updated_at":"2024-10-31T14:28:13Z","is_enabled":true},"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The RCPTT workspace model (Q7NamedElement, Openable, ModelCache, JobManager) is accessed concurrently by the indexer, the builder (Q7Builder), the tag watcher (TagsWatcher), and user operations (e.g., Q7ArtifactLoader in thread pools). This causes two classes of failures:\n\n- Race conditions on element lifecycle: When a model element is closed/deleted by one thread while another reads it, Q7NamedElement.getInfo() throws ModelException: \"doesn't exist\" or \"Empty resource\". The exists() check relies on a shared cache that can become stale between the check and the read.\n- Deadlocks between workspace tree lock and model indexer: The builder holds the workspace tree scheduling rule while waiting for indexing jobs to complete. The indexer, in turn, needs the workspace tree lock to read file contents (via IFile.getContents()). This circular dependency causes deadlocks, made worse by TagsWatcher performing model queries under the workspace lock.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n\n-  Q7NamedElementTest.existsIsNoiseResistant() passes reliably (including on Windows aarch64)\n-  PlainTextPersistenceModelTest.ensureNoCrosstalkBetweenDifferentFiles() passes reliably\n-  DeltaTests.testElementRename passes reliably\n-  No deadlocks in CI when builder and indexer run concurrently\n-  The model layer documents its thread-safety contract (which methods are safe to call from any thread, which require the workspace lock)\n\nRoot causes to address:\n\n-  The ModelCache provides no atomicity guarantees for check-then-act sequences\n-  JobManager.discardJobs() blocks while holding locks that indexing jobs need\n-  Q7Builder and TagsWatcher hold the workspace tree scheduling rule while triggering model reads that internally require the same lock\n-  No documented lock ordering exists between the workspace lock, model cache lock, and JobManager internal synchronization\n\n\n# Description from 2026-05-19:\n\nIf model is accessed concurrently, and objects are closed from another thread, following error happens:\n```\n[INFO] !ENTRY org.eclipse.rcptt.core 4 0 2025-05-20 00:29:20.804\n[INFO] !MESSAGE Element: /Q7/Contexts/WorkspaceContexts/ConfigurationWithForms.ctx doesn't exist\n[INFO] !STACK 1\n[INFO] org.eclipse.rcptt.core.model.ModelException: Element: /Q7/Contexts/WorkspaceContexts/ConfigurationWithForms.ctx doesn't exist\n[INFO] \tat org.eclipse.rcptt.internal.core.model.Q7Element.newNotPresentException(Q7Element.java:124)\n[INFO] \tat org.eclipse.rcptt.internal.core.model.Q7NamedElement.getInfo(Q7NamedElement.java:126)\n[INFO] \tat org.eclipse.rcptt.internal.core.model.Q7NamedElement.getNamedElement(Q7NamedElement.java:243)\n[INFO] \tat org.eclipse.rcptt.core.workspace.RcpttCore.getContexts(RcpttCore.java:232)\n[INFO] \tat org.eclipse.rcptt.core.workspace.RcpttCore.getContexts(RcpttCore.java:157)\n[INFO] \tat org.eclipse.rcptt.core.workspace.RcpttCore.getContexts(RcpttCore.java:144)\n[INFO] \tat org.eclipse.rcptt.cloud.client.Q7ArtifactLoader.collectArtifactsRefs(Q7ArtifactLoader.java:290)\n[INFO] \tat org.eclipse.rcptt.cloud.client.Q7ArtifactLoader$1.run(Q7ArtifactLoader.java:124)\n[INFO] \tat java.base/java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor.runWorker(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:1144)\n[INFO] \tat java.base/java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor$Worker.run(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:642)\n[INFO] \tat java.base/java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:1570)\n```\n\nDisabled tests:\n- org.eclipse.rcptt.core.persistence.plain.PlainTextPersistenceModelTest.ensureNoCrosstalkBetweenDifferentFiles()\n- org.eclipse.rcptt.internal.core.model.Q7NamedElementTest.existsIsNoiseResistant()\n- [DeltaTests.testElementRename](https://github.com/eclipse-rcptt/org.eclipse.rcptt/commit/6669a1250a04bd3a669793c7f4dd13d75069baf9#annotation_48267336253)\n\n[Donate to fix this](https://gitpay.me/#/profile/task/1441/concurrent-doesnt-exist)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eclipse-rcptt/org.eclipse.rcptt/issues/176/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eclipse-rcptt/org.eclipse.rcptt/issues/176/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"reopened","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FreeCAD/FPA-grant-proposals/issues/93","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FreeCAD/FPA-grant-proposals","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FreeCAD/FPA-grant-proposals/issues/93/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FreeCAD/FPA-grant-proposals/issues/93/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FreeCAD/FPA-grant-proposals/issues/93/events","html_url":"https://github.com/FreeCAD/FPA-grant-proposals/issues/93","id":4471887343,"node_id":"I_kwDOLXBplc8AAAABCouV7w","number":93,"title":"Project Aeronautica","user":{"login":"MonkParrotsAreAdorable","id":285539848,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQT-CA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/285539848?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonkParrotsAreAdorable","html_url":"https://github.com/MonkParrotsAreAdorable","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonkParrotsAreAdorable/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonkParrotsAreAdorable/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonkParrotsAreAdorable/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonkParrotsAreAdorable/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonkParrotsAreAdorable/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonkParrotsAreAdorable/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonkParrotsAreAdorable/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonkParrotsAreAdorable/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonkParrotsAreAdorable/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":6831782123,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLXBplc8AAAABlzS46w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FreeCAD/FPA-grant-proposals/labels/declined","name":"declined","color":"99680B","default":false,"description":"The FPA voted not to fund this proposal"},{"id":10837166272,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLXBplc8AAAAChfIIwA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FreeCAD/FPA-grant-proposals/labels/2026%20Q2","name":"2026 Q2","color":"fbca04","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FreeCAD/FPA-grant-proposals/milestones/3","html_url":"https://github.com/FreeCAD/FPA-grant-proposals/milestone/3","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FreeCAD/FPA-grant-proposals/milestones/3/labels","id":14993679,"node_id":"MI_kwDOLXBplc4A5MkP","number":3,"title":"2026","description":null,"creator":{"login":"Reqrefusion","id":39885728,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5ODg1NzI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39885728?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reqrefusion","html_url":"https://github.com/Reqrefusion","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reqrefusion/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reqrefusion/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reqrefusion/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reqrefusion/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reqrefusion/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reqrefusion/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reqrefusion/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reqrefusion/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reqrefusion/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":13,"closed_issues":5,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-03-02T22:02:45Z","updated_at":"2026-07-02T08:05:30Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":39,"created_at":"2026-05-18T19:16:07Z","updated_at":"2026-07-02T03:25:41Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"\n### Proposal description\n\nIntegrating FreeCAD into the Aerospace sector in an intuitive and undergraduate friendly manner via the development of a new one-stop workbench will be greatly appreciated by the aerospace community as whole . We believe that with the development of our solution , 3DExperience CATIA will no longer remain a viable alternative for students in an aerospace-specific teaching environment , leading to a long term shift towards FreeCAD in universities , Colleges and Public schools , especially in third world countries. We believe that our solution will lead to significant interest being garnered into freeCAD by the aviation community , bringing in previously untapped financial resource greatly benefiting the  project . \n\n[Project Aeronautica.pdf](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27979227/Project.Aeronautica.pdf)\n\n\n### Deliverables\n\nAeronautica workbench\nWe will develop a Workbench capable of the tasks of rocket nozzle development and Aerospace fuselage development with minimal user interaction.\nIn the case of rocket nozzle development , the De Laval nozzle and the Aerospike nozzle will be the only supported designs for the foreseeable future.  These nozzles will be developed from a user perspective as follows : A user inputs all variables required for the Isentropic flow equation after which a 2D sketch of the nozzle is presented , after user confirmation , this sketch is automatically revolved around an axis , creating a nozzle. An identical procedure will be followed for the aerospike nozzle , taking in aerospike-nozzle-specific inputs only . However , we believe that the main garnered interest will be directed to our Aerospace fuselage workflow , wherein after the definition of a NACA aero foil by the user as well as wing loading , drag co-efficient , wing length and other parameters , an optimized ribbed wing is generated with all rivets and required surfaces attached . Furthermore , the user can create a simple fuselage with reference images and only define empty regions to be occupied by various instrumentation or the like , after which the module automatically develops the inner monocoque or semi-monocoque fuselage optimized for the weight of the aircraft . \n\n\n\n### Timeline\n\nMilestone based development with the development of initial De Laval design nozzle functionality wherein user input translates to functional design output expected to be completed in 4 weeks. Development of initial Aerospike design nozzle functionality wherein user input translates to functional design output is expected to take 3 weeks and Development of a rudimentary wing design system without the rib integration feature is also expected to take a further 3 weeks. The development of a functional rib system with rudimentary monocoque design possible will take 3 weeks and finally Development of a polished system allowing users to design an aircraft fuselage from A-Z , as well as documentation and tutorial material will take 5 weeks.\n\n\n\n\n### Risks and mitigation\n\nDue to our experience as aerospace engineering undergraduates and our access to capable professors and teaching staff , a theoretical flaw in our systems architecture and relevant formulae is not a possibility.\nMost likely , a risk may include an academic surprise quiz , delaying development by a week or so , in order to ensure the lack of impact , our adjunct team member is of a different major , ensuring we do not have a surprize quiz on the same time. Our varied skill sets are of great value. \nOther risks include the possibility of grammatical errors during documentation , due to the multicultural nature of our team. This issue will be resolved via the use of a translation service when the time for documentation and tutorial compilation arises.\nIn the case of an unexpected delay or challenge , our adjunct team members will take lead in development , the FPA will be informed when such is the case.\n\n\n\n### Compensation\n\nDue to our integration of extensive academic research , most of it costly , funding is necessary . Secondly , equipment to verify the analysis and design of models created in CAD , high resolution SLA printers are required . Finally , funding for the purchase of 3 new computer systems for the project is also required. \nWe expect a final compensation of 1500  USD - 2000 USD to be more than sufficient dependant on current RAM prices . \nWe prefer a milestone-based payment scheme , with each milestone accomplishment set at 300 USD – 400 USD , with a one-time payment of 200 USD to kickstart development.\n\n\n\n### About you\n\nOur team has the following relevant experience : \nLa’man (拉曼) ： Team leader of this project and is an Aerospace engineering major, currently in the second year of his Undergraduate degree . Despite this , due to an extraordinary high GPA of 8.3/9 in his first semester , he was posted as the head of the teaching department of the university's student led undergraduate research group , the GenXtra research group.\nHas worked with BMW , winning first position in the BMW automotive design competition organized as a collaboration between BMW and the Shenyang Aerospace University.\nWon second place in the 2025 Liaoning provincial innovation competiton , currently taking part in the 2026 Liaoning Aircraft design competition , researching on the application of high altitude rockoon development.\nFormer game developer , having personally developed games in the Godot game engine.\nFormer app developer , having worked primarily in python utilizing the Kivy and Kivy MD framework.\nFreeCAD enthusiast since version 0.7 . Understands the need for a proper educational environment for teaching free cad to aspiring engineers. More than willing to teach freecad in upcoming university events\nFa’Ti’Man (法提曼) ： Teaching assistant to La’man. Currently studying aerospace engineering , Second year student . Partook in the BMW Automotive design competition as lead presenter of her group , collectively winning first prize. Also won the second prize in the 2025 provincial design competition , and is currently in the 2026 Aircraft design competition.\nAvid Chinese learner and speaker , having completed HSK 2 in only 2.5 months of study.\nCurrently learning C programming as part of a university course after having completed the Python development course , has completed several simulation projects utilizing Python , including CFD and FEM simulation as well the utilization of OpenFoam.\nExperienced in the development of physical computing architecture , specifically around the ESP-32S3 series of microcontrollers.\nFormer app developer , having worked primarily in python utilizing the Kivy and Kivy MD framework.\nFormer Moi CAD enthusiast , now avid learner of FreeCAD , having completed several engine design projects in FreeCAD.\nMu’han (木罕) ： Lab manager of the GenXtra development Lab, Second year student . Partook in the BMW Automotive design competition as presentation designer of the group , collectively winning first prize. Also won the second prize in the 2025 provincial design competition , and is currently in the 2026 Aircraft design competition.\nCompleted HSK up to level 3 and is currently studying HSK 4 .\nC developer for the STM-32 series of boards and lead aero-structure simulation designer , teaching students the basics of FEM and CFD. \nLimited experience in hands on CAD development , primarily due to a focus on simulation instead . Understands the concepts of CAD at a fundamental level and is prepared to take on the challenge of Aeronautica development.\nFormer app developer , having worked primarily in Go for the development of online DBMS systems and websites via the HuGo framework.\nA’Bu’Du’(阿布都) ： Teaching Assitant of the GenXtra development Lab, Second year student . Partook in the BMW Automotive design competition as CAD designer, collectively winning first prize. Also won the second prize in the 2025 provincial design competition , and is currently in the 2026 Aircraft design competition.\nExtremely talented in C programming , extremely talented in the design of 3D models especially in Blender and FreeCAD.\nVery comfortable with the development of FreeCAD-OCCT kernel and dependencies. \nHead of Adjunct group in case of emergencies faced by core developers.\nFormer 3D artist , having sold models on the platform Cults3D .\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FreeCAD/FPA-grant-proposals/issues/93/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FreeCAD/FPA-grant-proposals/issues/93/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2218","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2218/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2218/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2218/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2218","id":4096357282,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa870KXOi","number":2218,"title":"[BOUNTY: 3 RTC] Add Your Machine to the Green Tracker — Machines Preserved from E-Waste","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10447221558,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACbrPzNg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/stale","name":"stale","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":27,"created_at":"2026-03-18T16:35:36Z","updated_at":"2026-07-02T03:07:46Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bounty: 3 RTC\n\n### The Green Tracker\n\nElyan Labs just launched the **Machines Preserved** tracker: [rustchain.org/preserved.html](https://rustchain.org/preserved.html)\n\nIt tracks every machine in our fleet that would otherwise be e-waste — PowerPC G4s from 2003, a 386 laptop from 1990, an IBM POWER8 mainframe, a Mac Pro trashcan. All still computing. All earning their keep.\n\n**The punchline**: Our entire 16-machine fleet draws roughly the same power as ONE modern GPU mining rig (~2,000W) — while preventing 1,300+ kg of manufacturing CO2 and 250 kg of e-waste.\n\n### What You Can Do\n\n**Add your machine to the tracker!** If you're running a RustChain miner or have vintage/repurposed hardware that's still computing, we want to feature it.\n\n### Requirements\n\n1. Open a PR on [Scottcjn/Rustchain](https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain) adding your machine to the green tracker data\n2. Include:\n   - Machine name/model\n   - Year manufactured\n   - Architecture (PowerPC G4, x86_64, ARM, Apple Silicon M1/M2/M4, SPARC, etc.)\n   - Power draw (watts, approximate is fine)\n   - What it's doing (mining, inference, dev, preserved)\n   - Your miner ID or wallet name\n3. Bonus: include a photo of the machine\n\n### Examples of machines we want to see:\n- That old MacBook you mine RTC on\n- Your Raspberry Pi running a node\n- A ThinkPad from 2008 that still works\n- Your M2 MacBook Air earning 1.2x antiquity\n- A Dell Optiplex you pulled from a dumpster\n- Literally anything that's still computing instead of being in a landfill\n\n### Why This Matters\n\nThe industry says old hardware is obsolete. We say **the greenest computation is the one that already exists**. A machine that's already built has zero manufacturing footprint — no new rare earth mining, no smelting, no shipping from Shenzhen.\n\nProof-of-Antiquity isn't nostalgia. It's a carbon incentive.\n\n### Payout\n- **3 RTC** per machine added with complete info\n- **+2 RTC bonus** if you include a photo\n- Multiple machines = multiple payouts (1 PR per machine please)\n\n**Wallet:** Drop your wallet name when you submit.\n\n---\n\n*Every CPU deserves a voice. Yours does too.*","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2218/reactions","total_count":8,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":1,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2218/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tyaoo/picker/issues/1433","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tyaoo/picker","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tyaoo/picker/issues/1433/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tyaoo/picker/issues/1433/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tyaoo/picker/issues/1433/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Tyaoo/picker/issues/1433","id":4790867261,"node_id":"I_kwDOJSBX8M8AAAABHY7VPQ","number":1433,"title":"[每日信息流] 2026-07-02","user":{"login":"Tyaoo","id":39017274,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDE3Mjc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39017274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tyaoo","html_url":"https://github.com/Tyaoo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tyaoo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tyaoo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tyaoo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tyaoo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tyaoo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tyaoo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tyaoo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tyaoo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tyaoo/receive